%N A398431 a(n) is the least positive multiple of n that is a factorial base Niven number.
%C A398431 The sequence is well defined as factorial numbers are factorial base Niven numbers and each positive integer divides infinitely many factorial numbers.
%H A398431 Rémy Sigrist, <a href="/A398431/b398431.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398431 <a href="/index/Fa#facbase">Index entries for sequences related to factorial base representation</a>
%F A398431 a(n) <= A092495(n).
%F A398431 a(n) = A398496(n) * n.
%e A398431 The first terms are:
%e A398431   n   a(n)  A007623(a(n))  A034968(a(n))
%e A398431   --  ----  -------------  -------------
